  "music": "w2-sizzle-street",
  "authorNotes": "Solo. The belt is real now: belt-crossing (650,900 to 1550,900, speed 110) spans a 900px gap with no plank beneath it — the first true fall of the world, since staying gripped to a moving surface is exactly as demanding as gripping a static ledge would be. It lands flush on the mid counter. pan-mid (1700,860, 1.2s grace) is the world's first heat hazard, a hot spot embedded in the counter's own surface between the belt's landing and relic-w2-02 (2000,810) — cross it briskly (the grace period is generous, it will not kill an unlucky half-second) rather than lingering. Past the pan, grab the relic and take swing-final (pivot 2340,600, 260px) over the last stretch of void to the goal counter. The haul objective needs relic-w2-02 delivered, so the pan is not optional scenery — you must go through, or around its edge, to finish. One assist beam spans the final swing gap only; there is no beam over the belt itself, since it is solid footing, not a void crossing."
